.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8b/Vase_soliflore_MET_SF2006_83_img4.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Vase soliflore MET SF2006 83 img4","license":"CC0","creator":"Jean-Joseph Carriès","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vase_soliflore_MET_SF2006_83_img4.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Soliflore_en_%C3%A9mail_de_Longwy_268.2_13.jpg/960px-Soliflore_en_%C3%A9mail_de_Longwy_268.2_13.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/Soliflore_en_%C3%A9mail_de_Longwy_268.2_13.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Soliflore en émail de Longwy 268.2 13","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","creator":"Coyau","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soliflore_en_%C3%A9mail_de_Longwy_268.2_13.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"}],"links":{"studies":[],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Perfume - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfume"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Body odor & breath","chain":["Choose a perfume centred on one flower","Apply as part of grooming routine","Distinct, clean signature scent","Adds to overall presentation"],"effect":"indirect","text":"A soliflore adds a simple floral note to a grooming routine. It affects how a person smells rather than how they look."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Soliflore (French for 'single flower') describes a perfume dominated by the scent of one flower, for example rose, carnation or iris. Perfume classification lists it as the single floral family, and gives Serge Lutens's Sa Majeste La Rose as an example [1].","In grooming, a soliflore gives a clear, identifiable scent that wearers pick as a signature. Fragrance is part of the overall impression someone makes, so the connection to appearance is through presentation and scent rather than visible features."],"infobox":[["Type","Fragrance style (single floral)"],["Term origin","French, 'single flower'"],["Example","Sa Majeste La Rose (Serge Lutens)"],["Family","Floral"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["The Floral family is one of five main families on the fragrance wheel, alongside amber, woody, aromatic fougere and fresh. Within floral, a single floral is dominated by one flower, while a floral bouquet combines several, and a modern 'bright floral' category merges both styles [1].","Perfumes unfold in notes: top notes appear immediately and evaporate quickly, heart notes form the body, and base notes emerge about half an hour after application [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Perfume","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfume","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[]}